# The lines that mysqldump can write differently for a copy that usql made
# and a copy that mysqldump made. Each line below is a regular expression of
# Go, and a line of either dump that it matches is left out of the
# comparison.

# MariaDB stores a JSON column as LONGTEXT with a check of json_valid on the
# column. dbmeta writes the LONGTEXT and leaves the check out, so the copy
# takes any text. Reported to dbmeta on 2026-11-09, after v0.39.0.
^\s*`profile` longtext
